armstrongsubero — 4/26/26, 4:14 PM
Today was plyaing around wit dma stuff, I see the Baochip  has a PL230 MDMA DMA controller, tihs reads fine, reports 8 channels....but writes to the config registers silently fail, dug though the Xous codebase and found a comment abotu this haha...thank goodness!!  So I wrote a DMA engine in C using the BIO coprocessor instead, 700 MHz memory copies, dedicated BIO3 for this, it means when you're doing MDMA in bare metal C you can't use that BIO engine, but its totally worth it, the BIO is really a big help on this chip!
bunnie — 4/27/26, 12:02 AM
I think I eventually mangaed to figure out how to get something to work on the PL230 but it's tricky to configure and also closed source, so I decided not to support it driver-wise. The BIO (edit - i had said MDMA incorrectly here before) should have slightly better performnce than the PL230 when optimized but both have "meh" peak performance due to the slow speed of the bus they are connected to. 
armstrongsubero — 4/28/26, 7:59 AM
Finally got reliable readings from the adc, I didn't realize it taps out at bandgap reference (1.208v) and I thought I was doing soemthing wrong, was testing with a pot so saturation came quickly, lol, also to get DMA transfer to work correctly, you must set RX_CFG to 1 and you need to enable the adc after analog block enables and put a small delay to get it to stabilzie..the Daric SDK was useful for the init sequence.....but what no where tells you is that it's also its CRITICAL to use low impedance on input, I think could be the internal sampling cap, with high source impedance (I'm guessing) the cap cannot charge fast enough, and you get stale reading from internal leakage currents..to get usable (usable for me is able to read 0-3.3v liek other mcus) 3.2k or lower total impedance on input and you'll be fine...used a pot with voltage divider 2.2k and 1k and getting usable ADC readings....I guess if you're using an op amp you can skip the divider and connect correctly as long as the voltage is below the 1.208v bandgap reference I measured....
armstrongsubero — 4/29/26, 11:00 AM
This ReRAM thing is kinda cool, wrote a driver for unaligned support and readback verification, reminds me of the days when eeprom were on chip (for those of you who used old school 8-bitters), for some reason feels much eaiser to interact with compared to flash drivers on the chips I've used recently...I set it at around 2.5MB accessible by that so it wont collide with programs....4MB of memory is a LOT for bare metal...unless you're storing large binary blobs or something its hard to write even a 1 MB program lol.....oh also got an interrupt dispatch system up, Timer0 firing at 500 ms and UART TX done interrupts running simultaneously through the same VexRiscv trap handler....ended up being 20 IRQ arrays, each with 16 event sources, one callback table so shoudl be easy to use...as I work through will post more stuff here, more or less about 50% done....I can't think about anything else but this chip right now lol....
armstrongsubero — 5/2/26, 4:13 PM
