armstrongsubero — 5/7/26, 5:15 PM
So I've been heads down on this for a while now, finally got the bare metal C SDK to a point where I'm happy with it,  in total I have 17 drivers, 26 examples, and I tested all tested on hardware.... covers pretty much everything on the chip....What I have got up is GPIO, UART, SPI, I2C, PWM, ADC, timers, BIO, DMA, RRAM, AES, SHA, TRNG, WDT, RTC, QSPI, I also integrated W25Q and a FatFS example for SD cards. All UDMA based with blocking and async APIs where it makes sense, . Put it up on GitHub if anyone wants to poke at it, its not 100% complete but it's usable, I ran static analysis and stuff, but I'm sure bugs will popup though use, if you got any bugs tell me here, I'm working on a doc for this, should be up by next week, nothing fancy but like a reference guide....well here's the link to the repo over the next couple of weeks to months I'll be doing projects with this ship and I'll update the SDK as bugs pop up...

